      "notes": [
        {
          "on": "birchllc",
          "tone": "flag",
          "title": "No assignment of Birch Avenue LLC to the trust is in the documents.",
          "body": "It was formed in 2022, three years after the trust. Its agreement lists Sam as the only member (Sched. A) and its § 9.2, on a member’s death, names no successor. Unless a general assignment in the trust reaches it, it goes through probate when Sam dies. Before assigning it, the estate attorney checks the operating agreement and the loan, since a transfer can need the lender’s consent."
        },
        {
          "on": "ira",
          "tone": "ask",
          "title": "The documents don’t show a beneficiary for Dana’s IRA.",
          "body": "Ask the custodian for the current designation, so the plan on paper matches what would actually happen."
        }
      ],
      "gaps": [
        {
          "from": "birchllc",
          "zone": "in-trust",
          "label": "No assignment on file"
        }
      ],
      "kicker": "If you have a living trust and formed anything after it",
      "law": "Ownership as shown by deeds, operating agreements and account records. Ohio is a common-law property state, so title decides ownership between spouses."
    },
    {
      "id": "first-death",
      "type": "transfer",
      "fig": 1,
      "event": "sam-dies",
      "title": "When Sam dies, one rental would likely go through probate court.",
      "subtitle": "How each thing in these documents that Sam owns or controls would pass if Sam dies first and Dana survives. Only the LLC needs a court, unless a general assignment in the trust reaches it.",
      "recipients": [
        "dana",
        "trust"
      ],
      "order": [
        "brokerage",
        "k401",
        "life",
        "home",
        "elmllc",
        "birchllc"
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "on": "birchllc",
          "tone": "flag",
          "title": "Probate is the one route here that runs through a court.",
          "body": "Sam’s will leaves Birch Avenue LLC to the trust, but only after probate: a public court process with costs paid from the estate first. In Ohio the creditor claim period alone is six months. Until an executor is appointed, no one may have clear authority to run the rental. Fig. 2 shows why it is outside the trust."
        },
        {
          "on": "trust",
          "tone": "info",
          "title": "“No court” is not “nothing to do.”",
          "body": "Under trust Art. 6 the whole trust continues with Dana as sole trustee; many joint trusts instead split at a first death. A death still brings notices, date-of-death values and possibly an estate tax return to keep Sam’s unused exemption. Which part counts as Sam’s, for the basis step-up and estate tax, depends on the trust’s terms and who contributed what."
        },
        {
          "on": "dana",
          "tone": "ask",
          "title": "Any form that names Sam needs a new beneficiary.",
          "body": "After Sam’s death, Dana updates every beneficiary form that names Sam. Her IRA’s designation isn’t in the documents, so it is the first one to check."
        }
      ],
